<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Opening Get Started">
        <FluentText>
            Scan the QR code your manager shows you, or go to <strong>/get-started</strong> after you sign in. You can
            also open it from <strong>Account Management</strong> with <strong>Set up this device</strong> beside
            Notifications. When you set your password, <strong>Continue to Login</strong> takes you straight there once you've signed in.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            Each step shows a tick once it's done on the phone you're using, and the top of the page counts how many are finished. When the
            important ones are done you'll see <strong>You're all ready</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="1. Put the app on your Home Screen">
        <FluentText>
            This step only shows on a phone or tablet. On Android, select <strong>Install</strong> and confirm. If
            there's no Install button, follow the steps shown for your browser.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            On iPhone and iPad, follow the steps to <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>, then open the app from your
            Home Screen and open Get Started again from there. Notifications can only be turned on from the app,
            not from Safari.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="2. Turn on notifications">
        <FluentText>
            Select <strong>Turn on notifications</strong> and choose <strong>Allow</strong> when your phone asks. Then
            use <strong>Send me a test</strong> and answer whether it arrived. On a computer this step is optional.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="3. Face ID or fingerprint sign-in">
        <FluentText>
            Optional. Select <strong>Set Up on This Device</strong> so you can sign in with your face or fingerprint
            instead of typing your password. Your fingerprint and face never leave your phone.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Find your way around">
        <FluentText>
            The tiles at the bottom take you to the parts of Lanyard you'll use most, such as your Rota and Chat.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
